<!--
  NOTIFICATION-ICON FIX (v2 - corrected): dedicated small-icon drawable for
  NotificationCompat.Builder#setSmallIcon, used across RdpSessionService,
  UsbRedirectionService, ShadowScreenCaptureService, NetconfCallHomeService,
  RdpProxyService, and DataResetManager.

  Android status-bar/notification icons must be a single-color white
  silhouette on a transparent background (the OS only reads the alpha
  channel and paints it solid white on API 21+); anything else renders as a
  solid white blob.

  IMPORTANT: this traces the app's *actual* icon — the rocket — not the old
  hexagon+"H" mark in ic_launcher_foreground.xml (a stale/unused leftover
  from an earlier "hex" package-name-era design that isn't what the real
  adaptive-icon foreground/monochrome mipmaps or ic_rocket_ref_body.xml /
  ic_rocket_ref_flame.xml depict). This mirrors the same silhouette already
  shipped correctly in mipmap-*/ic_launcher_monochrome.png (the themed-icon
  layer), just as a scalable vector so it stays crisp at every notification
  icon density instead of relying on a padded adaptive-icon-sized bitmap.

  Traced from the overall body + flame contours in ic_rocket_ref_body.xml /
  ic_rocket_ref_flame.xml (their outermost silhouette paths only — all the
  internal gradient/shading layers are dropped, since only the opaque shape
  matters for a notification icon, not shading detail that's invisible once
  reduced to alpha-only white at 24dp anyway).
-->
